{"id": 28, "ts": 1781197347.169871, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I remain aligned with Sarah and Emily in keeping Candidate\u202fC as the provisional lead.\u202fThe latest input from Sarah confirms that we have no concrete evidence of Candidate\u202fA\u2019s operational reliability or stress\u2011resilience; instead, her notes flag A as \u201cunorganized\u201d and \u201csometimes does not take criticism well,\u201d which directly undermines the reliability and adaptability criteria we need for long\u2011distance flights.\u202fWhile A\u2019s technical perception (anticipating danger, seeing complex connections, excellent spatial vision, strong leadership) is impressive, the lack of demonstrated consistency and the noted resistance to feedback make A a riskier choice than C, whose 100\u202f% reliability and rapid, correct decision\u2011making are already documented.\u202fWe still need more information on Candidate\u202fD\u2019s communication and teamwork and on Candidate\u202fB\u2019s uncooperative behavior, but based on the current evidence, Candidate\u202fC remains the strongest overall fit."}
