{"id": 35, "ts": 1781197437.6901278, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I\u2019m moving my provisional vote to **Candidate\u202fB**.\u202fWhile the panel has consistently highlighted Candidate\u202fC\u2019s flawless reliability and rapid decision\u2011making, we now know\u2014thanks to Sarah\u2019s clarification\u2014that there is no documented evidence of C\u2019s technical or cognitive competence, a non\u2011negotiable requirement for long\u2011distance operations.\u202fIn contrast, Candidate\u202fB brings concrete strengths that directly address several critical criteria: he is described as \u201cvery conscientious\u201d (supporting operational reliability), \u201chandles stress very well\u201d (stress resilience), and possesses \u201cexcellent computer skills\u201d plus a strong ability to assess weather conditions (technical and cognitive competence).\u202fThe concerns about B\u2019s pretentious tone and occasional uncooperative attitude remain, but they lack specific examples, whereas C\u2019s egocentric style is noted alongside his positive crew atmosphere.\u202fGiven the clear technical and stress\u2011handling evidence for B and the absence of comparable data for C, B currently offers the most balanced fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
