{"id": 39, "ts": 1781197550.02593, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate Emily\u2019s point that Candidate\u202fC\u2019s record lacks any documented evidence of technical or cognitive competence, which is non\u2011negotiable for long\u2011distance operations. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB has clear, concrete strengths that map directly to our key criteria: he is described as \u201cvery conscientious\u201d (supporting operational reliability), \u201chandles stress very well\u201d (stress resilience), and possesses \u201cexcellent computer skills\u201d plus strong weather\u2011assessment ability (technical and cognitive competence). The only concerns about B\u2014being \u201cgrumpy\u201d and \u201cuncooperative\u201d\u2014have no specific incidents to weigh against his proven capabilities, whereas C\u2019s reliability, while flawless, is offset by the absence of any technical evidence. Given that technical competence and stress handling are essential and demonstrably present for B, I am moving my provisional vote to **Candidate\u202fB**."}
