{"id": 44, "ts": 1781197615.53582, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I concur with Emily and Sarah that Candidate\u202fB is the strongest provisional choice.\u202fHe has concrete evidence of operational reliability (\u201cvery conscientious\u201d), stress resilience (\u201chandles stress very well\u201d), and technical competence (excellent computer skills and strong weather\u2011assessment ability), all of which are non\u2011negotiable for long\u2011distance flights.\u202fIn contrast, Candidate\u202fC, while flawless on reliability, lacks any documented technical or cognitive competence; Candidate\u202fA has no evidence of reliability or stress handling and shows concerning resistance to feedback; Candidate\u202fD, although responsible, is noted for a hot temper and an arrogant, know\u2011it\u2011all attitude with no proof of effective crew cooperation.\u202fThe only lingering concern for B is the reported grumpy/uncooperative demeanor, but without specific incidents it does not outweigh his proven strengths.\u202fTherefore, I provisionally recommend Candidate\u202fB."}
